  "failure": {
    "body": "**THIS IS A BUG TARGETING the Debian 11 / Kernel 5.10 UPGRADE**\n\n#### Description\nThe packages `fdisk` and `gpg` are missing from the host image. They were previously present in buster.\n\nThis is currently breaking `fwutil` which assumes these packages will be present.\n\nManual installation of these packages fixes the `fwutil` flow.\n\n#### Steps to reproduce the issue:\n1. Run `show platform firmware status` on a Mellanox switch\n\n#### Describe the results you received:\n```\nError: Command 'mount -n -r -t ext4 /bin/sh: 1: fdisk: not found /mnt/onie-fs' returned non-zero exit status 1.. Aborting...\nAborted!\n```\n\n#### Describe the results you expected:\nShould return the expected output for this command."
  },
  "resolution": {
    "pr_number": 8191,
    "repository": "sonic-net/sonic-buildimage",
    "url": "https://github.com/sonic-net/sonic-buildimage/pull/8191",
    "title": "Upgrade SONiC to Debian Bullseye",
    "merged_at": "2021-11-10T23:27:23Z",
    "description": "#### Why I did it\n\nIn preparation for Debian Bullseye, upgrade SONiC's base system to be based on Bullseye, which was released in August 2021. Major changes from Buster are:\n\n1. Kernel is now based on 5.10.x (currently, official Debian Bullseye is publishing the 5.10.70 kernel)\n2. Most Python 2 packages (as well as `pip2.7`) have been removed from Bullseye. The Python 2 interpreter is still available.\n\n#### How I did it\n\nThe kernel has been upgraded to 5.10.46, and the base system is now based on Bullseye. Containers are still based on Buster.\n\n#### How to verify it\n\n#### Which release branch to backport (provide reason below if selected)\n\n- [ ] 201811\n- [ ] 201911\n- [ ] 202006\n- [ ] 202012\n- [ ] 202106\n\n#### Description for the changelog\n\n#### A picture of a cute animal (not mandatory but encouraged)",
